Variation:
This result is affected by the following factors;
* this data reflects a three year average, so despite an increase in active borrowers in the municipality in 2021/22, the overall result remains lower than previous years, and 
* the Alpine Shire population growth has risen faster than the rise in active borrowers so % borrowers is proportionally lower.

Road related requests increased from 224 to 309 in 2021?22. The increase was due to:
The Railway Level Crossing Removal Project (LXRP) related works have been started and a number of heavy vehicles using the local roads increased, causing damage to local roads; 
there is a reduction in investment on road projects; 
more travelling due to lifting the travel restrictions. However, the figure is consistent with pre-LXRP and pre-COVID period.

Kerbside collection is a schedule of rates contract and any movements in costs are adjusted in two ways: 
1. By CPI according to the All Ords Index which can rise or fall and;
2. By increasing or decreasing the number of bins collected.

